<tei:p><tei:pb n="676" ed="1949 sukkot rites" facs="https://archive.org/download/PhilipBirnbaumHaSiddurHaShalemTheDailyPrayerBook1949/page/n700_medium.jpg"/><tei:milestone unit="prayer-part" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:sukkot/text/ushpizin_enter"/>May it be thy will, Lord my God and God of my fathers, to cause thy divine spirit to dwell in our midst. O spread over us thy shelter of peace, and encircle us with thy majestic glory, holy and pure. As for those who are hungry and thirsty, do thou grant them sufficient bread and water. O grant us long life in the Holy Land, that we may serve thee with reverence. Praised be the Lord forever. Amen, Amen.<tei:milestone unit="prayer-part"/></tei:p>
